    ])
    // ONE impl block reached via TWO import paths (by-name + namespace alias): the alias emission
    // rewrites the body's module-local call to `sh__helper`, so the two flat copies are NOT
    // byte-equal — the resolver's impl dedup must key on ORIGIN identity and stay silent here.
    // std.rt (A) ambient default, ZERO setup: rt.alloc/rt.release serve from the heap default.
    // std.rt (B) with-INJECT: rt.with(counting_rt) makes 3 ambient allocs bump the counter to 3.
    // std.rt (C) TEST-inject: rt.with(failing_rt) makes an ambient alloc return null, observed inside.
    // std.rt (D) EARLY-RETURN restore (the save-set-restore trap): body early-returns 7 inside
    // with(failing_rt); AFTER the block the ambient is restored to the default, so an alloc there
    // SUCCEEDS (non-null). Exit 5 iff both hold — proves restore ran even on the early-return path.
    // ── UFCS through module aliases: x.f(a) resolves to alias__f by receiver type ────────────
    // `g = geo` + `g.Point(…).scale(2).norm1()` — the method chain resolves without flat imports.
    // `s = std.text.str` + `name.eq(…)` / `name.len()` — std fns as methods through the alias.
    // ── sibling import loading (test_user_imports) ──────────────────────────────────────────
    // ── namespace binds `x = mod` + qualified `x.fn()` (test_user_imports) ───────────────────
    // ── import-head spacing variants all resolve the sibling (test_modules_oracle) ───────────
    // ── std-export name collisions resolved by namespace binding (test_user_imports) ─────────
    // std.core.slice.dup / std.text.str.dup_bytes — two same-named exports, namespace-qualified.
    // ── audit C2: a TYPE reached via a module ALIAS keeps ONE canonical C identity ────────────
    // A qualified-alias type ref (`str.ParseError`) must mangle to the SAME C struct as the bare
    // name `num` consumes (`{ ParseError } = std.text.str`), so a `Result<_, str.ParseError>` that
    // mixes both import paths in one conditional unifies instead of "type mismatch in conditional".
    // the acceptance combo: map alias alongside a type-bearing str alias compiles + runs.
    // std.text.ascii.at vs a sibling `at`.
    // std.text.str.at and std.text.ascii.at both `at`, plus a sibling `at`.
    // std.mem ownership modules export the same constructor names — namespace binds keep distinct.
    // std.text.num.integer / float vs sibling integer/float.
    // std.text.num allocator + Result formatting.
    // std.concurrent.runtime sync/async vs sibling sync/async.
    // std.concurrent.actor cell.request survives an export-name collision with a sibling `cell`.
    // std.text.string + std.concurrent.actor coexist without a bare `new_in` arity collision (BUG #4).
    // std.core.slice dup/node_in coexist with std.text.str (loaded via fmt) without a dup_in collision (COLLIDE-1).
    // std.concurrent.cown buf/file vs sibling buf/file.
    // ── name-clash namespacing + transitive re-export as REAL projects (test_resolver_oracle) ─
    // ── test_resolver_fixes.py — driver-level run cases ──────────────────────────────────────
    // bug 2: namespace bind `c = std.io.c` + qualified call compiles AND runs.
    // the renamed std.internal.ast builders (dupx/eqx) actually run.
    // std.internal.ast's decl buffer uses an explicit allocator (Counting allocator observes the acquire/release).
    // ── compiler.resolve PUBLIC API, driven as Zen programs via `zenc run` (test_user_imports) ──
    // import_edges: structured edges with module/alias/namespace/start/next.
    // import_edges (Result): an allocator that fails after K acquires returns .Err; with enough budget, .Ok.
    // provided_symbols: imported / foreign / type / fn symbols with precise spans.
    // symbol_key_in: keyword-safe symbol key with a Result allocator path.
    // module_graph: import edges + symbol set with keyword-safe keys.
    // strip_ns_into preserves multi-line block comments while rewriting qualified calls.
    // ── stress: huge generated projects/sources resolve without recursive stack growth ───────
    // 240-decl user module imported through a 2-name head (symbol-consumer stress). want = v0()+v239() = 0+9.
    // 120-name import head validation (import-head stress). want = v0()+v119() = 0+9.
    // 700-edge import_edges walk (edge-walk stack stress); first/last edges verified.
    // 220-symbol provided_symbols + module_graph + decl_names stress (self-generating program).
    // 3500-call namespace rewriter (strip_ns_into) stack-growth stress (self-generating program).
    // 260-decl final-dedup (with a duplicate v0) handled without a recursive walk.
    // #66a: the day-one import-collision wall. Aliasing `std.text.string` (a module whose type's methods
    // shadow its own top-level fns) alongside `std.text.fmt` (which imports that type unqualified) USED to
    // surface a bare `type String does not implement Allocator` error deep inside fmt.zen with zero
    // attribution — it must now be rejected AT THE USER'S IMPORT LINE (first case). The second case is the
    // zero-over-rejection control: aliasing a NON-split module (`std.text.str`, plain UFCS free fns) with
    // the same fmt import must still compile — the check fires only on the split-name + bare-import pair.
    // HMap's internal seed constructor must not bind std.mem.raw.of after transitive flattening.
    // These sources differ only in import order; both orders must accept.
    // OWNERSHIP THROUGH A NAMESPACE BIND (last three cases): a sibling's consuming verb fn (`drop`
    // over an Rc) called QUALIFIED (`reslib.drop(r, a)`) flattens to `reslib__drop(r, a)` — the
    // consume matchers accept the `…__verb` alias suffix (sx_named), so the use-after-drop is
    // error[ownership] exactly like the brace-import spelling of the SAME program (the two import
    // styles must agree; regression pin for the bare-`eq` matcher hole). The zero-over-reject
    // control: an ns-aliased fn merely NAMED `release` (`mathlib__release` after flatten) over
    // NON-owner args must stay legal — the suffix match still gates on the first argument's
    // Own/Rc/Arc type, so plain code never trips the consume matchers.
    d := run_mod_verdicts("modules verdict (cross-module check / loader errors)", [
        ModVerdictCase(
            files: [
                ModFile(
                    name: "p.zen",
                    src: "{ Sys, Writer } = std.sys.root\n{ Result } = std.core.result\n{ HMap } = std.collections.hmap\nmain = (sys: Sys) i32 { 0 }\n",
                ),
            ],
            entry: "p.zen",
            should_pass: true,
            needle: "",
        ),
        ModVerdictCase(
            files: [
                ModFile(
                    name: "p.zen",
                    src: "{ HMap } = std.collections.hmap\n{ Sys, Writer } = std.sys.root\n{ Result } = std.core.result\nmain = (sys: Sys) i32 { 0 }\n",
                ),
            ],
            entry: "p.zen",
            should_pass: true,
            needle: "",
        ),
        ModVerdictCase(
            files: [
                ModFile(
                    name: "p.zen",
                    src: "string = std.text.string\n{ println } = std.text.fmt\n{ Malloc } = std.mem.alloc\nmain = () i32 {\n  m := Malloc(_: 0)\n  s := string.init(m.addr(), 16).expect(\"oom\")\n  println(\"ok\")\n  0\n}\n",
                ),
            ],
            entry: "p.zen",
            should_pass: false,
            needle: "error[import-collision]",
        ),
        ModVerdictCase(
            files: [
                ModFile(
                    name: "p.zen",
                    src: "s = std.text.str\n{ println } = std.text.fmt\nmain = () i32 { println(\"hi\") 0 }\n",
                ),
            ],
            entry: "p.zen",
            should_pass: true,
            needle: "",
        ),
        ModVerdictCase(
            files: [
                ModFile(
                    name: "x.zen",
                    src: "f* = (a: i32, b: i32) i32 { a + b }\n",
                ),
                ModFile(
                    name: "p.zen",
                    src: "{ f } = x\nbad* = () i32 { f(1, 2, 3) }\nmain = () i32 { bad() }\n",
                ),
            ],
            entry: "p.zen",
            should_pass: false,
            needle: "error[arity]",
        ),
        ModVerdictCase(
            files: [
                ModFile(
                    name: "x.zen",
                    src: "f* = (a: i32, b: i32) i32 { a + b }\n",
                ),
                ModFile(
                    name: "p.zen",
                    src: "{ f } = x\nbad* = () i32 { f(\"hi\", \"there\") }\nmain = () i32 { bad() }\n",
                ),
            ],
            entry: "p.zen",
            should_pass: false,
            needle: "error[arg-type]",
        ),
        ModVerdictCase(
            files: [
                ModFile(
                    name: "x.zen",
                    src: "f* = (a: i32, b: i32) i32 { a + b }\n",
                ),
                ModFile(
                    name: "p.zen",
                    src: "{ f } = x\ngood* = () i32 { f(1, 2) }\nmain = () i32 { good() }\n",
                ),
